Given:

O₂E (r2)= 2.4 cm

O₁D (r1) = 4 cm

Distance between centers (d) = O1O2 = 6.5 cm

Formula used:

Common tangent = √{d² - (r₁ - r₂)²}

Calculation:



 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/9d88ea4629d8b650dbd322d733ce05e48fc4c10979afc4221b119fbeeae9059a.png] 

Common tangent (DE) = √{d2 - (r1 - r2)2}

⇒ √{(6.5)2 - (4 - 2.4)2}

⇒ √{(42.25 - (1.6)2}

⇒ √{(42.25 - 2.56}

⇒ √39.69 = 6.3 cm

**∴ The correct answer is 6.3 cm.**

**Given:**

Radii of the circles are 9 cm and 4 cm.

**Formula Used:**

Length of common tangent, AB = sqrt{(r₁ + r₂)² - (r₁ - r₂)²}

**Calculation:**

Let r_1 = 9 cm and r_2 = 4 cm.

AB = sqrt{(9 + 4)² - (9 - 4)²}

AB = sqrt{13² - 5²}

AB = sqrt{169 - 25}

AB = sqrt{144}

AB = 12 cm

**The length of AB is 12 cm.**
